<title>FRANCE: Arianespace to launch British Skynet satellite.</title>
<headline>Arianespace to launch British Skynet satellite.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>European rocket consortium Arianespace will launch the British Skynet 4F telecommunications satellite in the second half of 1999 for Matra Marconi Space.</p>
<p>Arianespace said in a statement on Wednesday that Armand Carlier, chairman of Matra Marconi Space, a joint venture between GEC and Lagardere's Matra Defence Espace signed the agreement with Arianespace chairman Charles Bigot on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The satellite is the fourth entrusted to Arianespace by the British Ministry of Defence. Built by Matra Marconi Space, it has a seven-year lifespan and will operate government communications.</p>
</text>
